@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# IRON HRX host runtime
+
+This backend runs the artifacts emitted by `aiecc` (`final.xclbin` and
+`insts.bin`) through HRX instead of XRT:
+
+```bash
+IRON_RUNTIME=hrx python <example>.py ...
+```
+
+## Requirements
+
+- An HRX build with the amdxdna driver enabled.
+- An amdxdna NPU and driver.
+- `HRX_LIBHRX`, `LIBHRX_DIR`, or `HRX_INSTALL` when HRX is not installed in a
+  standard location.
+
+The runtime supports Linux and Windows. It discovers `libhrx.so` or `hrx.dll`
+and calls the public HRX C API through `ctypes`.
+
+## Executable creation
+
+IRON does not serialize XADX or link FlatCC. It passes:
+
+- the xclbin bytes,
+- the raw XAie transaction from `insts.bin`, and
+- the entry-point name
+
+to `hrx_amdxdna_executable_create`. HRX derives host relocation metadata from
+the transaction, serializes its private XADX representation, and loads the
+executable. This keeps the backend package format and schema implementation
+inside HRX and avoids a platform-specific helper library.
+
+## C++ examples
+
+Programming examples can select the same backend with:
+
+```bash
+HRX_INSTALL=/path/to/hrx-install RUNTIME=hrx make run
+```
+
+`hrx_test_wrapper.h` uses the same `hrx_amdxdna_executable_create` API and links
+only against the installed `hrx::hrx` package. `HRX_INSTALL` is unnecessary
+when that package is already on CMake's normal search path.
+
+## Files
+
+- `discovery.py`: cross-platform HRX shared-library discovery.
+- `__init__.py`: HRX C ABI bindings and `HRXContext`.
+- `hostruntime.py`: IRON `HostRuntime` implementation and executable cache.
+- `tensor.py`: HRX-backed tensor storage and cache synchronization.
